title: El terreno de cada pueblo
max-visits: 1
view-if: 0
# Container/namespace only. EIGHT TOWNS, EIGHT BATTLES. Contact is resolved by the ground it
# happens on: every village in this sierra has one thing in it that a guerrilla can use and a
# battalion cannot, and knowing what that thing is — for each place — is what four years of
# living here is actually worth. Each of these overrides the generic @la_batalla for its node.
# Every one is a chain: local opening -> a decision inside the local trick -> foco_batalla.bat_fin.
#
# bat_bonus is the value of knowing your own ground. bat_plan reuses the shared families so the
# resolution maths in foco_batalla stays single-sourced.

# =====================================================================
# ACAPULCO — the port. Nine hundred thousand people, a naval station, and the tourists.
# =====================================================================
@bat_acapulco
title: Contacto en Acapulco
new-page: true
face-image: img/anti-guerillas.jpg
subtitle: The deepest garrison in the state, and the only place with a crowd to disappear into
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and ej_contacto = 1 and cerco_total = 0 and col_nodo = "acapulco" and time >= bat_last + 2
priority: 11
frequency: 100
max-visits: 8
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_last=Q.time; Q.bat_plan=""; Q.bat_res=""; Q.bat_terreno=-12; Q.bat_bonus=0; !}

= Contacto en Acapulco

The worst ground in Guerrero to be caught on, and you knew that when you came down here.

This is the port: a naval station, the 27th's barracks, the airport, four thousand men in uniform within twenty minutes of anywhere, and behind all of it a city of tourists that the Republic cares about in a way it has never once cared about a village. Every road out has a checkpoint on it because every road out always has a checkpoint on it. There is no sierra to climb into. There is a beach.

And there is the one thing the sierra does not have: nine hundred thousand people, most of them poor, packed into colonias on the hills behind the hotels where no soldier goes willingly and no map is accurate.

- @bat_ac_colonia: **La colonia.** Up into the barrios on the hill — the unpaved, unmapped, unpoliceable city. *(the only real cover here; you become an urban problem)*
- @bat_ac_hotel: **Cruzar por la zona turística.** Straight through the tourist strip, where they will not fire. *(audacious; the state's own vanity as cover)*
- @foco_batalla.bat_dar: **Dar la cara.** Fight in the port. *(here, against this garrison — read that sentence again)*
- @foco_batalla.bat_romper: **Romper hacia la carretera.** Out along the coast road toward Coyuca and the sierra beyond.

@bat_ac_colonia
new-page: true
face-image: img/neza.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse"; Q.bat_bonus=14; !}

= Arriba, entre las casas

You go up. Within four hundred metres the asphalt stops and the city becomes what the city actually is: a hillside of block and cardboard and rebar, no street names, no plan, thirty thousand people who arrived from the sierra in the last fifteen years and were never counted by anybody.

They know exactly who you are within the hour. That is not a metaphor — half these families are from Atoyac and Tecpan, and several of them have relatives in your column.

- @bat_ac_c_casas: Split up into houses and let the colonia hide you until the sweep passes. *(their risk, entirely)*
- @bat_ac_c_pasar: Keep moving straight through and out the back of the hill by dawn. Do not make them choose. *(harder; nobody else pays)*

@bat_ac_c_casas
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_ligero"; Q.bat_bonus=20; Q.f_cerco+=6; Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+6; !}

@bat_ac_c_pasar
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_pesado"; Q.bat_bonus=12; var _h=Math.max(0,(Q.apoyo_techo||55)-(Q.apoyo_popular||0)); Q.apoyo_popular+=Math.min(4,_h*0.25); !}

@bat_ac_hotel
new-page: true
face-image: img/guadalajara1970s.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse"; Q.bat_bonus=6; !}

= La Costera

The idea is so stupid that it takes the column four minutes to understand you are serious: walk out along the Costera Miguel Alemán, in daylight, in front of the hotels, among people from Texas in sunglasses.

They cannot shoot here. The entire economy of this state is thirty metres to the left, drinking something with fruit in it, and there is not an officer in Mexico who will authorize a firefight in front of it.

- @bat_ac_h_calma: Walk it. Slowly. Like people who belong on a seafront. *(nerve alone; every second is a lifetime)*
- @bat_ac_h_ruido: Make it a spectacle — leaflets, a banner off the hotel front, the war on the front page. *(they will have to answer for it; the manhunt becomes national)*

@bat_ac_h_calma
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_ligero"; Q.bat_bonus=10; !}

@bat_ac_h_ruido
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_pesado"; Q.bat_bonus=2; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+5; Q.legitimidad_regimen-=6; Q.pol_intl=(Q.pol_intl||0)+10; Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+12; Q.f_cerco+=14; !}

# =====================================================================
# COYUCA — the lagoon. Water, mangrove, and boats the army does not have.
# =====================================================================
@bat_coyuca
title: Contacto en Coyuca
new-page: true
face-image: img/anti-guerillas.jpg
subtitle: Between the highway and a lagoon nobody has ever mapped properly
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and ej_contacto = 1 and cerco_total = 0 and col_nodo = "coyuca" and time >= bat_last + 2
priority: 11
frequency: 100
max-visits: 8
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_last=Q.time; Q.bat_plan=""; Q.bat_res=""; Q.bat_terreno=-6; Q.bat_bonus=0; !}

= Contacto en Coyuca

Coyuca is a trap with a door in it.

The trap is the geography: the town sits pinned between the coast highway and the lagoon, which means the army has a road on one side and open water on the other and only has to close two ends. They know this. It is why they came here.

The door is that the lagoon is not open water at all. It is forty square kilometres of mangrove channel that changes with the tide and has never been surveyed by anyone but the men who fish it, and there are ninety families in this town who own a boat and have every reason to dislike the federal government.

- @bat_co_laguna: **La laguna.** Into the mangroves with the fishermen. *(the army has no boats and no chart; the fishermen are exposed forever after)*
- @bat_co_carretera: **La carretera.** Break across the highway and into the cane before they can close it. *(fast; open ground for ninety seconds)*
- @foco_batalla.bat_dar: **Dar la cara.** Fight in the streets of the town.
- @foco_batalla.bat_filtrarse: **Filtrarse.** Out in threes through the cane at night.

@bat_co_laguna
new-page: true
face-image: img/agua_neza.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse"; Q.bat_bonus=16; !}

= Entre los manglares

Eleven boats come out of eleven different places without anybody having been asked twice, poled rather than rowed because a rowlock makes noise, and the column goes into the mangrove in the dark at the top of the tide.

Inside the channels it is absolutely black and absolutely silent and completely safe, and a helicopter over the top of it sees a green roof. The army will be on the shore by first light with binoculars, looking at a wall of leaves.

- @bat_co_l_fondo: Deep in, and sit there for four days until they get bored. *(safe; four days of no food and no news)*
- @bat_co_l_cruzar: Straight across and out the far side tonight, and gone before they think of the far side. *(fast; the far side may already be thought of)*

@bat_co_l_fondo
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_ligero"; Q.bat_bonus=24; Q.f_comida-=12; Q.f_moral-=4; !}

@bat_co_l_cruzar
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_pesado"; Q.bat_bonus=12; !}

@bat_co_carretera
new-page: true
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="romper"; Q.bat_bonus=-4; !}

= Cruzar la carretera

Ninety seconds of asphalt with nothing on it, and then two metres of cane and you are invisible again. Ninety seconds is a very long time.

- @bat_co_c_noche: Wait for full dark and cross in one rush. *(the obvious moment; they know it too)*
- @bat_co_c_camion: Stop a bus, put it across the road, and cross behind it. *(the civilians on the bus have no vote in this)*

@bat_co_c_noche
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="romper_todos"; Q.bat_bonus=2; !}

@bat_co_c_camion
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="romper_guardia"; Q.bat_bonus=14; Q.brutalidad=(Q.brutalidad||0)+1; Q.apoyo_popular-=3; !}

# =====================================================================
# ATOYAC — the town where the sierra meets the road. Lucio's town. Market day.
# =====================================================================
@bat_atoyac
title: Contacto en Atoyac
new-page: true
face-image: img/anti-guerillas.jpg
subtitle: The town this whole war came out of
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and ej_contacto = 1 and cerco_total = 0 and col_nodo = "atoyac" and time >= bat_last + 2
priority: 11
frequency: 100
max-visits: 8
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_last=Q.time; Q.bat_plan=""; Q.bat_res=""; Q.bat_terreno=-2; Q.bat_bonus=0; !}

= Contacto en Atoyac

Atoyac de Álvarez, where the road ends and the mountain starts, and where in May 1967 the police fired into a parents' meeting outside the school and turned a village teacher into a guerrilla. Everything that has happened since happened because of a morning in this square.

Which means two things at once. It means the garrison here is permanent and reinforced and hates you personally. And it means that of the people standing in this square right now, a substantial number were standing in it that morning too.

It is Thursday. The market is on. Four hundred people, awnings, animals, sacks, and a crowd it would take a company an hour to move.

- @bat_at_mercado: **El mercado.** Go out through the market at the busiest hour and let the town be the terrain. *(they cannot shoot into it; the town chooses whether to close around you)*
- @bat_at_escuela: **La escuela.** Out past the school where it started, up the arroyo behind it into the coffee. *(the ground everyone in this column knows by heart)*
- @foco_batalla.bat_dar: **Dar la cara.** Fight for Atoyac. *(in the town the movement was born in, in front of everyone)*
- @foco_batalla.bat_romper: **Romper hacia la sierra.** Up and out, the way you always go.

@bat_at_mercado
new-page: true
face-image: img/elpueblo.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse"; Q.bat_bonus=8; !}

= Jueves de plaza

You go in among the awnings in ones, rifles under blankets and inside sacks of maize, and the market does the thing a market does, which is close over you like water.

Nobody says anything. A woman moves a crate. Someone's grandmother starts a very long and very loud argument with a soldier about the price of chillies at precisely the moment it is useful. This is not organization. This is four hundred people independently making the same decision in the same four minutes.

- @bat_at_m_salir: Out the back of the market and gone, and let the town keep its Thursday. *(the town is not touched; you take nothing with you)*
- @bat_at_m_hablar: Before you go — up on a crate, in the middle of the market, and speak. *(the whole town hears the movement's voice; every informer in it hears it too)*

@bat_at_m_salir
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_ligero"; Q.bat_bonus=18; !}

@bat_at_m_hablar
