Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+4; Q.legitimidad_regimen-=4; Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+8; Q.f_cerco+=10; !}

@bat_at_escuela
new-page: true
face-image: img/cards/escuela.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="romper"; Q.bat_bonus=12; !}

= Por la escuela

The arroyo behind the primary school runs up into the coffee and from the coffee into the sierra, and every person in this column over the age of twenty-five has walked it, most of them as children, several of them on the eighteenth of May 1967 with the shooting behind them.

You do not need a guide. You do not need light.

- @bat_at_e_rapido: Straight up and out. Speed. *(the ground does the work)*
- @bat_at_e_esperar: Wait in the coffee above the school and hit whatever follows you into the arroyo. *(the ambush your childhood laid out for you)*

@bat_at_e_rapido
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="romper_todos"; Q.bat_bonus=16; !}

@bat_at_e_esperar
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="dar_punto"; Q.bat_bonus=22; Q.f_parque-=8; if(Q.f_parque<0){Q.f_parque=0;} !}

# =====================================================================
# SAN VICENTE — coffee country. The beneficio, the drying patios, the pickers.
# =====================================================================
@bat_sanvicente
title: Contacto en San Vicente
new-page: true
face-image: img/anti-guerillas.jpg
subtitle: Coffee country, in the middle of the harvest
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and ej_contacto = 1 and cerco_total = 0 and col_nodo = "sanvicente" and time >= bat_last + 2
priority: 11
frequency: 100
max-visits: 8
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_last=Q.time; Q.bat_plan=""; Q.bat_res=""; Q.bat_terreno=2; Q.bat_bonus=0; !}

= Contacto en San Vicente

Coffee country, and it is the harvest, which changes everything.

Coffee grows under shade — old trees, dense, two and a half metres of leaf in every direction, visibility of about nine metres and no line of sight for anything. It is the best infantry cover in the state and it goes on for forty square kilometres. A man can stand four metres from you and see leaves.

It is also full of people: three hundred pickers working the rows, whole families, sacks and ladders and children, half of them migrants from Oaxaca who have no idea who anybody is and are not going to be a witness to anything.

- @bat_sv_cafetal: **El cafetal.** Into the coffee and let the shade trees do it. *(the finest cover in Guerrero; three hundred civilians in it)*
- @bat_sv_beneficio: **El beneficio.** The processing works — concrete, water tanks, drying patios, and the only defensible building for nine kilometres. *(a real position; you are fighting for a rich man's factory)*
- @foco_batalla.bat_filtrarse: **Filtrarse.** Out in threes at night through the rows.
- @foco_batalla.bat_romper: **Romper hacia arriba.** Up toward El Porvenir and out of reach.

@bat_sv_cafetal
new-page: true
face-image: img/countryside2.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse"; Q.bat_bonus=18; !}

= Bajo la sombra

Forty metres in and the war becomes a question of hearing rather than seeing. You can hear a company moving through coffee from a very long way off, because coffee is noisy and men in webbing are noisier, and they cannot hear you at all because you are moving at the speed of somebody picking.

The pickers keep picking. Some of them move a ladder in a way that is not about the ladder.

- @bat_sv_c_pickers: Move with the pickers — same pace, same rows, sacks on the shoulder. *(indistinguishable; if it fails, it fails on them)*
- @bat_sv_c_solos: Away from the rows where the people are, out through the empty sections. *(slower and more exposed; nobody else is in it)*

@bat_sv_c_pickers
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_ligero"; Q.bat_bonus=24; Q.estado_intel=(Q.estado_intel||0)+4; !}

@bat_sv_c_solos
