= Contacto en El Quemado

This is the village that got burned. Everyone here has already paid once for the crime of your existence, and the arithmetic of what happens next is being done, very fast, behind two hundred pairs of eyes.

The track ends here — this is the last place a truck reaches, which is why they can come at all and why they cannot follow you out. Above the village the limestone starts, and in the limestone there are caves that the whole valley has used to hide things in since before anyone was keeping records.

- @bat_eq_cuevas: **Las cuevas.** Up into the limestone, with the village if they will come. *(a fortress the army cannot enter; you are choosing the whole village's fate for it)*
- @bat_eq_evacuar: **Sacar al pueblo primero.** Fight nothing. Get every human being out of the houses before the troops reach them. *(you take no shot; the village survives, and knows why)*
- @foco_batalla.bat_dar: **Dar la cara.** Fight in front of them, on their ground, for their village.
- @foco_batalla.bat_romper: **Romper hacia Río Chiquito.** Up the vereda into country the road cannot reach.

@bat_eq_cuevas
new-page: true
face-image: img/sierra_larga.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="dar"; Q.bat_bonus=22; !}

= La caliza

The caves go back further than anybody has ever gone, there is water in them, and the approach is a single goat path with a hundred and fifty metres of open rock in front of it. Two people could hold it. You have considerably more than two.

The question is who else goes up.

- @bat_eq_c_pueblo: Take the village up with you. Everyone. *(they are safe and they are besieged with you)*
- @bat_eq_c_solos: The column only. Tell the village to stay in its houses and be visibly, provably uninvolved. *(they may be believed; they may not)*

@bat_eq_c_pueblo
