# =====================================================================
# EL PORVENIR — the high side-trail. Cloud.
# =====================================================================
@bat_elporvenir
title: Contacto en El Porvenir
new-page: true
face-image: img/anti-guerillas.jpg
subtitle: Two thousand metres, in cloud, with no road for eleven kilometres
tags: event
view-if: banda = "sierra" and f_phase = "marcha" and ej_contacto = 1 and cerco_total = 0 and col_nodo = "elporvenir" and time >= bat_last + 2
priority: 11
frequency: 100
max-visits: 8
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_last=Q.time; Q.bat_plan=""; Q.bat_res=""; Q.bat_terreno=18; Q.bat_bonus=0; !}

= Contacto en El Porvenir

Whoever is on this ground walked here, which tells you a great deal about them before you see one of them.

Two thousand metres. The cloud comes up the valley at about four in the afternoon every single day of the year and by five you cannot see your own hands, and it does not lift until nine the next morning. There is no road within eleven kilometres. Nothing is being resupplied and nothing is being reinforced and no helicopter is landing in this, and whatever is up here is up here alone with you and running on what it carried.

That cuts both ways, and it cuts sharper for them: they have eleven days of rations and you have a mountain full of people who feed you.

- @bat_ep_niebla: **Esperar la niebla.** Do nothing until four o'clock, then fight or move inside the cloud. *(the weather as a weapon; nobody can see anything, including you)*
- @bat_ep_hambre: **Dejarlos sin comer.** Do not fight at all. Shadow them, cut their route back, and let eleven days become fourteen. *(the patient answer; it takes a fortnight and total discipline)*
- @foco_batalla.bat_dar: **Dar la cara.** Fight them here, above the cloud line.
- @foco_batalla.bat_romper: **Romper hacia Río Chiquito.** Deeper in.

@bat_ep_niebla
new-page: true
face-image: img/sierra_larga.jpg
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="dar"; Q.bat_bonus=16; !}

= A las cuatro de la tarde

It comes up the valley exactly on time, the way it has every day since before any of this, and inside twenty minutes the world is nine metres wide and completely silent and full of soldiers who cannot see each other.

Fighting in this is a coin toss for a formation and a home advantage for people who have lived in it for four years.

- @bat_ep_n_atacar: Go into them inside the cloud, close, where the mortars and the radio are useless. *(brutal, intimate, decisive)*
- @bat_ep_n_pasar: Do not touch them. Walk out through the middle of them in the cloud and be eleven kilometres away by morning. *(no result; no cost)*

@bat_ep_n_atacar
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="dar_punto"; Q.bat_bonus=24; !}

@bat_ep_n_pasar
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse_pesado"; Q.bat_bonus=26; !}

@bat_ep_hambre
new-page: true
choose-if: disciplina >= 60 and f_comida >= 25
unavailable-subtitle: Shadowing a unit for two weeks without being drawn into a fight, and feeding your own people while you do it, needs discipline of 60 and food in hand.
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="filtrarse"; Q.bat_bonus=10; !}

= Once días

You do not fight them. You walk where they walk, a ridge over, for eleven days, and you take the two places they would have to come out through, and you wait.

It is the least dramatic operation in the column's history and by day nine you can see it in the way they are moving.

- @bat_ep_h_rendicion: On the fourteenth day, offer them terms: leave the weapons, walk out, nobody dies. *(a bloodless disarmament; some of the column will hate it)*
- @bat_ep_h_golpe: On the fourteenth day, when they are finished, hit them. *(a starved unit is a destroyed unit)*

@bat_ep_h_rendicion
go-to: foco_batalla.bat_fin
on-arrival: {! Q.bat_plan="dar_perimetro"; Q.bat_bonus=30; Q.f_parque+=14; Q.leyenda=(Q.leyenda||0)+5;
Q.legitimidad_regimen-=5; Q.pol_intl=(Q.pol_intl||0)+8; Q.brutalidad=(Q.brutalidad||0)-1; if(Q.brutalidad<0){Q.brutalidad=0;} !}

@bat_ep_h_golpe
